# BMW 1-series F70 five-door hatchback, 2024 onwards.
#
# The fourth 1-series: the front-wheel-drive UKL2 car with the revised nose,
# the flush door handles and the mild-hybrid range. UK order books opened
# 4 June 2024, first deliveries October 2024.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_1_Series_(F70)
#
# Dimensions 4.361 x 1.800 x 1.459 m, wheelbase 2.670 m.
#
# Shape reference: the pack's images show the five-door in side, front and
# rear views; the side view governs.
#
# Colours: grade (c), names evidenced for the F70: Alpine White, Black
# Sapphire, Skyscraper Grey and M Portimao Blue. Weights 9, 8, 7, 6, total
# 30, provisional.
#
# Speed 225 km/h. Comfort 88/312, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 88. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 2024 intro, retires staggered 2046-2049.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-1-series-f70.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-1-series-f70.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bmw-1-series-f70/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the model does not fully reproduce the F70's diagonal
# grille pattern or the lower rear bumper shape. At 128 px the revised nose,
# flush handles and five-door body read as an F70.


obj=citycar
name=BMW1SeriesF70(AlpineWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=9
intro_year=2024
intro_month=10
retire_year=2049
retire_month=6
speed=225
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=88
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=312

